course: dictionary
lesson: 10206
title: Tiptoe: walking quietly and carefully
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Tiptoe is a verb. You tiptoe when you walk quietly on the front parts of your feet, with your heels off the ground. Context gives clues: ask yourself why someone would walk like that. Usually it is to be quiet, so as not to wake someone, or to reach something high.
explain: The word also appears in phrases. «On tiptoe» means standing or walking on your toes, often to reach higher. «Tiptoe around» means to avoid talking about something difficult, so it does not mean walking at all.
explain: Check the sentence to see which meaning fits. «Picture Ling drawing a horse whose legs look wrong: she checks a photo and sees that the joint that bends "backwards" is really the horse's ankle, because horses walk on tiptoe.» Here tiptoe describes how a horse's feet touch the ground, not a quiet walk.
fact: Tiptoe means to walk quietly and carefully on the front parts of your feet, with your heels off the ground.
fact: «On tiptoe» or «on tiptoes» means standing or walking on your toes, often to reach higher.
fact: «Tiptoe around» means to avoid talking about something difficult.
fact: Safety: stretching up on tiptoe on a wobbly chair is dangerous, so ask an adult for help or use a proper step.
fact: «An elephant walks on its tiptoes», with a big fatty pad behind the toes.
exercise: Hanna wants to be quiet so she does not wake the baby. How might she walk? | Stomp loudly across the floor | Run and jump | Shout to say hello | *Tiptoe across the room
exercise: «Picture Ling drawing a horse whose legs look wrong.» Why does the joint look like it bends backwards? | *Because horses walk on tiptoe, so that joint is the ankle | Because the horse is asleep | Because Ling drew it upside down | Because horses have no ankles
exercise: Which phrase means standing on your toes to reach a high shelf? | Sit still | Tiptoe around | Stamp about | *On tiptoe
test: What does «tiptoe around» mean? | *To avoid talking about something difficult | To stretch up to a high shelf | To walk very loudly | To dance on your toes
test: Why is stretching on tiptoe on a wobbly chair dangerous? | *You could fall, so ask for help or use a proper step | It makes the chair louder | It is not dangerous at all | Chairs cannot wobble
exam: Which sentence uses tiptoe to mean walking quietly? | Ling draws a horse | Dad gets home from work | The elephant walks on its tiptoes | *She tiptoes out of the room so she does not wake the baby
